eries is from 2025."}],"lineCount":9,"maximumDepth":2},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Should we expect v2 (re)based on recent tree?"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks\nDavid"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"[1] https://github.com/sm7150-mainline/linux/commit/7ea41523c678e94a7c048936052b5b1b1b109cdd"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Neil"},{"depth":1,"text":">>"},{"depth":2,"text":"Best regards,"},{"depth":2,"text":"Jens"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "}],"lineCount":5,"maximumDepth":2}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"283096ad-ae1b-42b8-8312-b192f735fc80@linaro.org"},"b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org":{"id":"b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org","messageId":"b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org","references":["20250422-sm7150-upstream-v1-0-bf9a9081631d@jiaxyga.com","2ca2b774-fd7f-4612-b38d-f60e32ff6f9a@mainlining.org","283096ad-ae1b-42b8-8312-b192f735fc80@linaro.org","cce3fe36-322e-49ed-8928-3aef813faad7@ixit.cz"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Danila Tikhonov","address":"danila@mainlining.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"David Heidelberg","address":"david@ixit.cz"},{"name":"Jens Reidel","address":"adrian@mainlining.org"},{"name":"Danila Tikhonov","address":"danila@jiaxyga.com"},{"name":"Miro Mraz","address":"mraz.miro@seznam.cz"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-watchdog@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-usb@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-phy@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-mmc@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"netdev@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-scsi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dmaengine@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-crypto@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-clk@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"iommu@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"","address":"linux-remoteproc@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"name":"","address":"neil.armstrong@linaro.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-hardening@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux@mainlining.org"},{"name":"Connor Mitchell","address":"c.dog29@hotmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T20:54:41.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T20:54:41.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 00/33] Add support for Qualcomm Snapdragon SM7150 SoC and Google Pixel 4a","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi David,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thank you for your comment."},{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 12/08/2026 14:40, David Heidelberg wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"On 23/04/2025 09:26, Neil Armstrong wrote:"},{"depth":2,"text":"Hi,"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"On 23/04/2025 00:07, Jens Reidel wrote:"},{"depth":3,"text":"Hi everyone,"},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"apologies for the mess this created. Danila's mail provider >>> ratelimited him halfway through sending the series and the attempt >>> to re-try sending the second half an hour later ended up with a new >>> message ID (I think due to not using --in-reply-to)."},{"depth":3,"text":"He asked me to let you know that this will be resolved later and the >>> whole series will be re-sent once the problems are resolved."},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"The b4 web submission is a great alternative when the mail provider >> is rate limited:"},{"depth":2,"text":"https://b4.docs.kernel.org/en/latest/contributor/send.html#web-endpoint"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I see people interested in moving Pixel 4a forward, but it seems this > was never upstreamed? I looked at sm7150 repository [1] where I see > FROMLIST, but these patches never arrived to the list and this series > is from 2025."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Should we expect v2 (re)based on recent tree?"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":19,"maximumDepth":3},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I'd definitely like to get back to upstreaming SM7150 and the devices\nbased on it, but I don't think there's much value in continuing with\nthis particular series as-is. A lot has changed in the kernel over the\npast year, which would require substantial changes throughout the series\nand would effectively force the maintainers to review it from scratch\nanyway."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I'd also like to split the series up to avoid targeting such a large\nnumber of maintainers in a single submission. Hopefully, I'll be able to\nfind some time to work on this in the near future."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Thanks"},{"depth":1,"text":"David"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"[1] > https://github.com/sm7150-mainline/linux/commit/7ea41523c678e94a7c048936052b5b1b1b109cdd"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"Neil"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"Best regards,"},{"depth":3,"text":"Jens"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":""}],"lineCount":12,"maximumDepth":3},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"---\nBest regards,\nDanila"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"cce3fe36-322e-49ed-8928-3aef813faad7@ixit.cz","parentId":"cce3fe36-322e-49ed-8928-3aef813faad7@ixit.cz"},"7B026D92-3826-494D-B1A9-EF01D41B4461@ixit.cz":{"id":"7B026D92-3826-494D-B1A9-EF01D41B4461@ixit.cz","messageId":"7B026D92-3826-494D-B1A9-EF01D41B4461@ixit.cz","references":["b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"David Heidelberg","address":"david@ixit.cz"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Danila Tikhonov","address":"danila@mainlining.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Jens Reidel","address":"adrian@mainlining.org"},{"name":"Danila Tikhonov","address":"danila@jiaxyga.com"},{"name":"Miro Mraz","address":"mraz.miro@seznam.cz"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-watchdog@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-usb@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-phy@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-mmc@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"netdev@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-scsi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dmaengine@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-crypto@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-clk@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"iommu@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"","address":"linux-remoteproc@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"name":"","address":"neil.armstrong@linaro.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-hardening@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux@mainlining.org"},{"name":"Connor Mitchell","address":"c.dog29@hotmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-13T09:20:11.000Z","iso":"2026-08-13T09:20:11.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 00/33] Add support for Qualcomm Snapdragon SM7150 SoC and Google Pixel 4a","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"On 12. 8. 2026, at 22:54, Danila Tikhonov <danila@mainlining.org> wrote:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"﻿Hi David,"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Thank you for your comment."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"On 12/08/2026 14:40, David Heidelberg wrote:"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"On 23/04/2025 09:26, Neil Armstrong wrote:"},{"depth":3,"text":"Hi,"},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"On 23/04/2025 00:07, Jens Reidel wrote:"},{"depth":4,"text":"Hi everyone,"},{"depth":4,"text":""},{"depth":4,"text":"apologies for the mess this created. Danila's mail provider ratelimited him halfway through sending the series and the attempt to re-try sending the second half an hour later ended up with a new message ID (I think due to not using --in-reply-to)."},{"depth":4,"text":"He asked me to let you know that this will be resolved later and the whole series will be re-sent once the problems are resolved."},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"The b4 web submission is a great alternative when the mail provider is rate limited:"},{"depth":3,"text":"https://b4.docs.kernel.org/en/latest/contributor/send.html#web-endpoint"},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"I see people interested in moving Pixel 4a forward, but it seems this was never upstreamed? I looked at sm7150 repository [1] where I see FROMLIST, but these patches never arrived to the list and this series is from 2025."},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"Should we expect v2 (re)based on recent tree?"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I'd definitely like to get back to upstreaming SM7150 and the devices"},{"depth":1,"text":"based on it, but I don't think there's much value in continuing with"},{"depth":1,"text":"this particular series as-is. A lot has changed in the kernel over the"},{"depth":1,"text":"past year, which would require substantial changes throughout the series"},{"depth":1,"text":"and would effectively force the maintainers to review it from scratch"},{"depth":1,"text":"anyway."}],"lineCount":33,"maximumDepth":4},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"After longer period of time maintainers will have to do full review anyway. Sure, the reviews needs to be addressed :)"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I'd also like to split the series up to avoid targeting such a large"},{"depth":1,"text":"number of maintainers in a single submission."}],"lineCount":3,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Yes, that’s exactly what’s needed (at least for the part patches I saw)."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Hopefully, I'll be able to"},{"depth":1,"text":"find some time to work on this in the near future."}],"lineCount":2,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Where the most recent patchset can be found? Just in case someone wanted to push some bits in meantime."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks\nDavid"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"Thanks"},{"depth":2,"text":"David"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"[1] https://github.com/sm7150-mainline/linux/commit/7ea41523c678e94a7c048936052b5b1b1b109cdd"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"Neil"},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":4,"text":""},{"depth":4,"text":"Best regards,"},{"depth":4,"text":"Jens"},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":"Best regards,"},{"depth":1,"text":"Danila"}],"lineCount":17,"maximumDepth":4}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":2,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org","parentId":"b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org"}},"rootIds":["cce3fe36-322e-49ed-8928-3aef813faad7@ixit.cz"],"childrenByParent":{"cce3fe36-322e-49ed-8928-3aef813faad7@ixit.cz":["b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org"],"b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org":["7B026D92-3826-494D-B1A9-EF01D41B4461@ixit.cz"]},"chronologicalIds":["cce3fe36-322e-49ed-8928-3aef813faad7@ixit.cz","b15b2687-0c2e-43b2-ac9e-78e04e77e065@mainlining.org","7B026D92-3826-494D-B1A9-EF01D41B4461@ixit.cz"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}